**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The constructor window holds its kit's items, read when the kit opens and when it reloads (the S7.1 mapper's request: read `KitProxy.readItems` on open; 001 §O 'Items panel: the list'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`: `OpenedKit` (steps 150, 184) gains `items : Item list` after `experiments`, documented in one line: the kit's items as read at open, in label order. The private `openedOver` (step 172) reads `readItems ()` (step 218) after `readExperiments ()`; a refusal closes the kit and is the answer, as any failed read is (step 150), so a kit with an unreadable item file is never left locked. `withRebindings` keeps it. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `kitItems : Item list` beside the kit's loaded content (step 187), documented in one line: the kit's items in label order, as the kit last read or wrote them; `initWith` sets it to `[]`. The private function of a kit's content that `loadKit` and `ReloadKitChanges` share (step 187 (4)) takes the items after the experiments and sets `kitItems`: `loadKit` passes `opened.items`; `ReloadKitChanges` reads `model.kit.proxy.readItems ()` after `readExperiments ()`, its `Error e` keeping the model and the offer with step 187's text; the copy message introduced in step 225 MUST pass the model's kitItems. A changed item file is offered for reload by step 130's check, because `.item-json` is a kind of `KitFileKind.all` (step 123). The doc of `loadKit` says, in no more words, that it loads the items. No other field or message changes. Tests. `KitOpeningTests` (step 150) gains `opening a kit reads its items, and an item file that does not read refuses the open`: a kit holding CPL1 and LP1, written through `writeItem` (step 218) and closed, answers `items` CPL1 then LP1 when opened again read-write and read-only; a kit whose `Broken.item-json` the test writes as `{` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitFileRejectedErr _)` naming it, and its folder holds no `.oc/lock`. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184) gains `a loaded kit's items are the window's, and Reload reads an item another writer wrote`: `initMain ()` loaded from a folder kit holding CPL1 holds `kitItems` CPL1; after another writer (step 187's `KitProxy.create` over the folder) writes LP1 through `writeItem`, `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnActivation` offers `LP1.item-json`, and `ReloadKitChanges` leaves `kitItems` CPL1 then LP1.

**Acceptance.** After the window holds items, `OpenedKit.items` MUST hold the kit's items read at open, a kit with an unreadable item file MUST not open, and `loadKit` and `ReloadKitChanges` MUST set `kitItems`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `opening a kit reads its items, and an item file that does not read refuses the open` and `a loaded kit's items are the window's, and Reload reads an item another writer wrote`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
